    "summary": "Explosive New Haven show with a blistering Wheel→Other One chain and killer Althea",
    "review": "New Haven's Veterans Memorial Coliseum saw the Dead unleash a late‑summer burst on September 23, 1982. The first set kicks off with an over‑driven \"Alabama Getaway\" that quickly settles into a tight groove, delivering a standout \"Althea\" where Jerry’s electric solo cuts through the mix and his vocal urgency shines. Little Red Rooster glides in with a crisp, bluesy tone, while Brent Mydland’s organ adds warm texture throughout. The second set launches into a soaring \"Touch of Grey\" before the band dives into an unforgettable sequence: \"The Wheel → The Other One → Wharf Rat,\" each transition locked in and full of improvisational fire. The debut of \"Throwing Stones\" lands with punch, followed by a thunderous post‑drum jam that showcases Bill Kreutzmann and Mickey Hart as true rhythm devils. The show closes on a high note with the rocking \"Johnny B. Goode\" and a tender encore, \"It's All Over Now Baby Blue,\" leaving the crowd buzzing long after the lights went down.",
